  "discharged": [
    "Actual original local fixed-determinant unramified representations lift along every surjective local finite coefficient-ring map, for prescribed continuous unramified determinant compatible with the residual determinant. Frobenius and the fixed-determinant matrix lift are constructed, not assumed.",
    "Original local norm inertia restricts trivially to the retained finite unramified factor.",
    "Each same selected prime has residually trivial inertia, with no new inertia hypothesis.",
    "Original unramified trace-zero H1 classes identify with actual continuous fixed-determinant unramified lifts modulo strict conjugacy.",
    "The same family kills original dual Selmer and has actual fixed-determinant unramified first-order dimension equal to the symmetric degree.",
    "The same original rational-prime completion has norm-residue cardinality p by transport of the existing native original-residue theorem.",
    "For an original finite number-field restriction with its literal embedding square, actual norm inertia in the finite quotient has a constructed normal p-group wild subgroup and a tame generator with Frobenius conjugation t -> t^p and prime-to-p tame order. Frobenius, the contracted prime, uniformizer, tame character and wild-order bound are constructed.",
    "The existing native Artinian residual matrix p-group theorem kills this wild subgroup for residual-unramified coefficient-q deformations when p differs from q. Their actual finite inertia image is cyclic and their Frobenius and inertia matrices satisfy the tame power relation."
  ],
  "boundary": "DUB-17 Theorem 2.6 and DUB-18 Corollary 8.2 still require the actual modular residual representation with its image and coefficient realization, ramified Taylor-Wiles local rings and their Delta_Q action and quotient comparison, higher-weight crystalline conditions and dimensions, Hecke freeness, compatible arithmetic patching, automorphy and descent to higher symmetric-power continuation. The finite tame and matrix equations are necessary local conditions; their converse realization and the arithmetic ring/module comparison are not proved by these equations. Acceptance remains 16/20; DUB-17-20 open.",
